{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1698","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. 3SUM Closure"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a$$$ of length $$$n$$$. The array is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3SUM-closed"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if for all distinct indices $$$i$$$, $$$j$$$, $$$k$$$, the sum $$$a_i + a_j + a_k$$$ is an element of the array. More formally, $$$a$$$ is 3SUM-closed if for all integers $$$1 \\leq i \\lt j \\lt k \\leq n$$$, there exists some integer $$$1 \\leq l \\leq n$$$ such that $$$a_i + a_j + a_k = a_l$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine if $$$a$$$ is 3SUM-closed."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 1000$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\leq n \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ ($$$-10^9 \\leq a_i \\leq 10^9$$$) — the elements of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ across all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) if $$$a$$$ is 3SUM-closed and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in any case (for example, strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will be recognized as a positive response)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n3\n-1 0 1\n5\n1 -2 -2 1 -3\n6\n0 0 0 0 0 0\n4\n-1 2 -3 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nNO\nYES\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, there is only one triple where $$$i=1$$$, $$$j=2$$$, $$$k=3$$$. In this case, $$$a_1 + a_2 + a_3 = 0$$$, which is an element of the array ($$$a_2 = 0$$$), so the array is 3SUM-closed."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, $$$a_1 + a_4 + a_5 = -1$$$, which is not an element of the array. Therefore, the array is not 3SUM-closed."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, $$$a_i + a_j + a_k = 0$$$ for all distinct $$$i$$$, $$$j$$$, $$$k$$$, and $$$0$$$ is an element of the array, so the array is 3SUM-closed."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1698C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1698/problem/C"}